cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "fortran_rationals: exact rational numbers with checked arithmetic"
type: software
abstract: >-
  fortran_rationals is a Fortran module, rationals, with the derived type
  rational: an exact fraction with a 64-bit numerator and denominator, always
  in lowest terms. It overloads the arithmetic and comparison operators and
  the numeric and array intrinsics, so a rational behaves like a numeric type.
  Every operation checks for integer overflow and stops instead of returning
  a wrong value; comparison uses continued fractions and never overflows.
  Reals convert to the simplest fraction that converts back exactly, and text
  converts both ways. It is Fortran 2018 and builds with fpm or make.
authors:
